;; iq2xs-dequant.fk — GGUF type 17 (IQ2_XS), authored from the BML layout contract.
;;
;; Qwen3.8-Flash-Next UD-Q2_K_XL contains 94 IQ2_XS tensors and zero Q2_K tensors. The
;; filename's family label therefore cannot select the decoder. This cell lowers the exact
;; 74-byte / 256-weight block named by iq2xs-layout.bml:
;;   d f16 @0..1 · qs u16[32] @2..65 · scales u8[8] @66..73.
;; A packed qword uses bits 0..8 as a 512-entry grid index and bits 9..15 as a 128-entry
;; sign index. Each scale byte supplies a low nibble to l=0/1 and a high nibble to l=2/3.
;;
;; AUTHORING HEIGHT. Address and bit-field meaning is authored in
;; form-stdlib/bml/iq2xs-layout.bml and crystallized as iq2xs-layout-xtal.fk. This raw cell
;; is its CPU lowering. The 4096-byte trained magnitude table remains raw constant data
;; because form.bml cannot yet carry a field this large without flattening it into authored
;; low-level noise; that is the named BML gap, not a preference for .fk.
;;
;; The grid is the 512 uint64 iq2xs_grid table in llama.cpp b10686 commit 3173a56, expanded
;; in little-endian host order. Its 4096-byte SHA-256 is
;; 06e47aaca60b4dc1d9b5a3f34540437058a6b142b4d7a59d5ded769b4d1bf1de.
;; ksigns_iq2xs is shared with the existing IQ2_XXS carver through iq2-ksigns.
;;
;; RADIUS. Pure CPU/list proof carver. The performance path is the sibling MSL fused
;; dequant/matvec lowering; this cell exists so GPU arithmetic has an independently readable
;; Form answer and never becomes self-certified device text.
;;
;; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/format-arith.fk form-stdlib/f16-decode.fk form-stdlib/iq2xxs-dequant.fk form-stdlib/iq2xs-layout-xtal.fk
;;
;; Proven by: form-stdlib/tests/iq2xs-dequant-band.fk

